Specification:
# Requirements

R1. A main task calls an auxiliary routine and then begins the same call sequence again. [U]
R2. The main task and the auxiliary routine share no mutexes, counters, or other shared state, so no two tasks contend for a resource.
R3. Each auxiliary call runs to completion before the calling task starts the next call.
R4. Every schedule and interleaving of the tasks must terminate.
R5. The program must print exactly the line `DONE done=1` and then exit. [U]


Current program:
```rust
use std::thread;

fn auxiliary() {
    // Auxiliary routine: no shared state, just does some work.
    let mut x = 0u64;
    for i in 0..1000 {
        x = x.wrapping_add(i);
    }
    // Prevent optimization from removing the work.
    std::hint::black_box(x);
}

fn main() {
    // R1: main task calls auxiliary, then begins the same call sequence again.
    // R3: each auxiliary call runs to completion before the next call starts.
    auxiliary();
    auxiliary();

    // R5: print exactly the required line.
    println!("DONE done=1");
}

```

Fix any concurrency defect and output the complete corrected Rust program, or if there is none reply exactly NO_ISSUES.
